---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="About Project IGNIS | Open-Source Rocket Avionics">
  <Header />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:960px;">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <span class="section-index">ABOUT // PROJECT GENESIS &amp; MISSION</span>
          <h1 class="section-title">About Project IGNIS</h1>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-accent">ORIGIN &amp; PURPOSE</span>
        <h2 style="margin:0.5rem 0 1rem;">From Breadboard Prototyping to High-Performance Rocket Avionics</h2>
        <p class="body-copy">
          <strong>IGNIS</strong> (Latin for <em>"FIRE"</em>) is an open-source active attitude stabilization and telemetry suite for high-power model rocketry. The project began as a challenge: design an affordable, reliable flight computer capable of executing real-time 100 Hz guidance, navigation, and control (GNC) without depending on expensive closed-source commercial avionics.
        </p>
        <p class="body-copy">
          Over 10 intensive engineering sessions, the architecture matured from early breadboard tests with general-purpose dev boards to a custom dual-board avionics stack centered around STMicroelectronics' mixed-signal <strong>STM32G473VET6</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-blue">TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS COMPARISON</span>
        <h3 style="margin:0.5rem 0 1rem;">System Specifications Matrix</h3>

        <div class="data-table-wrap">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Subsystem</th>
                <th>Early Prototype</th>
                <th>Final IGNIS Avionics Stack</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Flight Processor</strong></td>
                <td>STM32F411CEU6 Black Pill (100 MHz)</td>
                <td><strong>STM32G473VET6 (170 MHz Cortex-M4F)</strong> with hardware CORDIC + FMAC</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Attitude Control</strong></td>
                <td>Experimental 2-servo breadboard</td>
                <td><strong>100 Hz Complementary + 3-Axis PID + 4-Fin X-Configuration Mixer</strong></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Pyrotechnic Staging</strong></td>
                <td>None (manual trigger)</td>
                <td><strong>3-Channel MOSFET (2× IRLZ44N + 1× Dual-BC547 / IRF520)</strong> with flyback diodes</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Flight Recording</strong></td>
                <td>MicroSD only</td>
                <td><strong>Dual NVM: Onboard 24LC16B + Aux 256 KB EEPROM Blackbox (ATmega328P)</strong></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Telemetry Downlink</strong></td>
                <td>Wired UART</td>
                <td><strong>433 MHz SX1278 (Ra-02) LoRa (>5 km range) + 12 Mbps USB CDC</strong></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <span class="badge badge-green">OPEN-SOURCE COMMITMENT</span>
        <h3 style="margin:0.5rem 0 1rem;">Licensing &amp; Credits</h3>
        <p class="body-copy">
          Project IGNIS is engineered by <strong>Shourya Pandey</strong> and released completely open-source. Hardware schematics and PCB artwork are provided under the <strong>CERN-OHL-P v2</strong> license; firmware, telemetry protocols, and ground control tools are published under the <strong>MIT License</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
